# Target C — C76 exact mechanical star-face collapse

**LEVEL I STATUS: STILL OPEN.**

Full proof: [target_c_exact_mechanical_star_face_collapse_2026-08-31.md](../../reports/target_c_exact_mechanical_star_face_collapse_2026-08-31.md).

For any normalized KKT stress `s` and diameter vertex `z`, let

`S_z(s)=sum_(zk in H) beta_zk`.

For `D>=20`, C76 proves that the exact face `S_z=1` is not a generic mechanical star.

C68 applied to arbitrary normalized stresses gives `S_z=1 -> Q_z=0`. Hence every positive contact attains equality in the reverse triangle inequality for distance from `z`; every component of the positive contact support after deleting `z` lies on one ray and has one physical port.

C12 applies to every normalized stress. Summed equilibrium over one radial branch shows that each positive branch must contain a positive `z`-star diameter partner.

Two different branches would have distinct unit contact ports separated by at least `pi/3`. But C18 gives, for `D>=20`, a common diameter-star cone of width strictly below `pi/3`. Therefore only one branch exists.

The unique ray has only one source point at radius `D`, so

`H_s={za}`, `beta_za=1`.

Connected unit contacts along that ray force `D` to be an integer and the positive contact support to be exactly the `D`-edge straight chain from `z` to `a`. Equilibrium forces every chain contact stress to equal `D`.

Thus the KKT-polytope face

`{s:S_z(s)=1}`

is either empty or a singleton straight-chain stress.

## Effect

C66-C74 should now be read as convergence toward one straight-chain KKT vertex, not toward an arbitrary star network. Concurrent C75 independently forces any near-capacity quadratic core into a weight-free near-triangular missing-diagonal rhombic bulk.

The remaining obstruction is the uniform incompatibility of those two limits: a stress certificate collapsing to a one-dimensional chain while the source geometry retains a quadratic two-dimensional near-triangular carrier.

## Next target

Exploit the full KKT polytope or C75 geometry. Either force a transverse certificate with nonvanishing mixing weight, or prove an exposed straight-chain stress face cannot coexist with the C73/C75 near-capacity bulk in a global minimizer.